        "Stephen E. Harris",
        "Lene Vestergaard Hau"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Electromagnetically induced transparency made coherent control of optical propagation experimentally tangible and opened major routes to slow light and quantum memories.",
        "attribution": "Harris established the central EIT physics, while Hau supplied a landmark demonstration of extreme slow light and its experimental potential.",
        "maturity": "The underlying coherence phenomena are firmly established and have shaped quantum-optical interfaces and precision spectroscopy for decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Credit is distributed across foundational theory, early experiments, and later quantum-memory implementations."
        ]
