        "David E. Pritchard",
        "Mark A. Kasevich"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Atom interferometry created a powerful class of quantum sensors for inertial measurement and precision tests of fundamental physics.",
        "attribution": "Bordé developed foundational atom-interferometric concepts, Pritchard advanced precision atomic measurements, and Kasevich delivered defining interferometric demonstrations and applications.",
        "maturity": "The techniques are mature, quantitatively validated, and now underpin a substantial international precision-measurement field.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The broad history of atom interferometry makes a three-person attribution necessarily selective."
        ]
      }
    },
