        "Harald Rose",
        "Maximilian Haider",
        "Knut Urban"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Aberration correction removed a central limit of electron microscopy and made routine sub-angstrom imaging a transformative materials-physics instrument.",
        "attribution": "Rose supplied essential corrector theory; Haider and Urban were central to practical realization and demonstration in electron microscopy.",
        "maturity": "Corrected instruments are reliable, widely deployed, and indispensable across condensed-matter and materials research.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Several further engineers and microscopists contributed materially to commercial and experimental implementation."
        ]
      }
    },
